WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.638
Young cassava grows slowly. The first three to four months decide your harvest.

00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.583
Fill any gaps where cuttings failed.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.233
Keep the field weeded until the leaves cover the ground.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.661
Where you can, add compost or manure to improve poor soil.

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.302
Walk the field every week, and look for sick plants.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:26.444
Before you move on, check: Fill any gaps. Weed in the first months. Inspect plants every week.

00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:30.479
In the next lesson: Spotting and managing problems.
